{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded 7.7% a year from $15.4 billion in FY2018 to $25.8 billion in FY2025 [F1][F8][F145], while operating income grew faster at 9.9% [F146] and net income barely moved at 0.4% [F147]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The window is a growth-and-build story with two violent swings: operating margin fell 14.6pp in FY2021 to 15.5% [F20][D107], then jumped 23.5pp in FY2023 to 41.3% [F22][D177]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2021 collapse came with a $1.5 billion Mountain Valley Pipeline impairment in FY2020 and unfavorable non-qualifying hedge activity in FY2021 [P63][P68]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2023's margin spike reflected $1,729 million of non-qualifying hedge gains in NEER's net income [P30], a swing that reversed in FY2024 when NEER's results fell on unfavorable hedge activity [P36]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "FPL remains the revenue base at 70.5% of FY2025 revenue [D271], contributing 5.5pp of the 9.8% growth [D273][D236]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FPL's FY2025 revenue rose $1,243 million on higher storm cost recovery, retail base and storm protection plan revenues, partly offset by lower fuel cost recovery [P21]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "NEER's segment net income rose from $285 million in FY2022 [S26] to $2,975 million in FY2025 [S29], while FPL's reached $5,012 million [P23]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "NEER's FY2025 increase came from new wind, solar and battery investments, partly offset by higher financing costs [P26][P13]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew 10.7% against 9.8% revenue growth in FY2025 [D237][D236], but operating costs grew 10.0% [D249], so there was no operating leverage."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "FY2025 operating margin of 32.1% [F24] sits 1.8pp above the 30.3% window median [D300] but well below the 41.3% FY2023 high [D299]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "D&A rose to 25.5% of revenue in FY2025 from 23.2% [D224][D189], the main cost pressure, while stock-based compensation stayed at 0.7% [D223]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "D&A expense increased $951 million in FY2025, mainly higher amortization of deferred storm costs from Hurricanes Debby, Helene and Milton [P16]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net margin fell 3.1pp to 26.5% [F40][D248] even as operating margin edged up 0.3pp [D247], because other income (expense) was -$3,750 million [X64]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Corporate and Other's results fell $1,256 million, largely on about $1,002 million of unfavorable non-qualifying hedge activity and higher average debt balances [P8]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $12.5 billion was 1.83x net income in FY2025 [F64][F32][D227], below the 1.95x window median [D319]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow fell 5.8% [D241] while investing outflow reached $23.9 billion [F72], so free cash flow was deeply negative and funded by $23.4 billion of debt issued [X90]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The shift from net over-recovery to net under-recovery of cost recovery clauses cut FPL's operating cash flow by about $89 million in FY2025 [P19]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Stock-based compensation is immaterial to cash at 1.5% of operating cash flow [D228], so conversion is driven by working capital and the capital programme, not equity pay."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net debt widened for a seventh straight year to $92.2 billion in FY2025 [D231][R2], equal to 357.4% of revenue [D232]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "That leverage ranks at the 0th percentile against three utilities peers, whose median net debt is 235.4% of revenue [D328][D329]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Liquidity is thin: cash of $2.8 billion [F96] against a 0.60x current ratio [F128], the window high but still below 1.0x [D305]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow shortfalls were met with debt and $4.7 billion of dividends [D233][X82], while the diluted share count rose 0.6% [D251]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net debt has risen every year of the window, from $34.3 billion in FY2018 to $92.2 billion in FY2025 [D9][D231], the most persistent concern [R2]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The current ratio of 0.60x is below 1.0x [F128][R1], though it is the strongest level in the window [D305] and typical for a utility funding long-lived plant with short-term paper."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2025 effective tax rate of -17.7% [D226] reflects NEER's clean energy tax credits, which rose about $585 million [P11], so the low rate is structural rather than an accounting error [R4]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "FY2019 operating expenses were later restated to $14,257 million from $13,851 million [X18][R5], a data-quality caveat on that year's cost comparisons."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Watch whether operating margin holds above the 30.3% window median [D300]; a drop toward the 15.5% FY2021 low [D298] would signal hedge losses or cost pressure returning."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Watch net debt against the FY2025 level of $92.2 billion [D231]; further growth at the 15.7% FY2025 pace [D253] would extend the seven-year streak [R2]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Watch operating cash flow conversion against the 1.95x window median [D319]; a print below the 0.99x FY2018 low [D318] would flag working-capital strain."}
  ]}
]}
